{
    "background_story": "Francisco was a talented artist who had always dreamed of showcasing his work in the city's prestigious galleries. However, after years of struggling to make a name for himself, he found himself stuck in a mundane office job to make ends meet. As he watched his friends and acquaintances achieve success and recognition, Francisco couldn't help but feel resentfully towards the art world that seemed to have passed him by. He felt like he was wasting his talent and creativity, forced to suppress his true passion in order to pay the bills. Despite his frustration, Francisco continued to paint in secret, his brushstrokes fueled by a mix of anger and longing. His art became a reflection of his inner turmoil, a testament to the sacrifices he made for the sake of stability.",
